@startuml
participant "Alice\nlanlink-client-reader" as AR
participant "Alice\nlanlink-file-sender" as AS
participant "Server worker\nlanlink-‹id› (Alice)" as SA
participant "Server worker\nlanlink-‹id› (Bob)" as SB
participant "Bob\nlanlink-client-reader" as BR

note over AR, BR : Start: transfer ACCEPTED, chunks flowing (see Figure 7)

alt Alice disconnects in the middle of the transfer
  AS -[#C0392B]-> SA : TCP connection closes
  note over SA
  receive() returns None
  (EOF) or raises OSError
  end note
  note over SA
  _serve_client finally:
  remove alice from _users,
  state CLOSED
  end note
  note over SA
  _fail_transfers_of
  (CONNECTION_LOST) →
  _fail_transfer_and_notify:
  FAILED, session deleted
  end note
  SA ->> BR : ERROR CONNECTION_LOST (transfer_id)
  note over BR
  Receiver.handle_message
  → _fail_and_cleanup:
  .part deleted, FAILED
  end note
else hash mismatch at the end
  AS ->> SA : FILE_END
  SA ->> BR : FILE_END (total_chunks,\ntotal_bytes)
  note over BR
  Receiver.finish:
  SHA-256 ≠ offer.sha256
  → HASH_MISMATCH,
  .part deleted, FAILED
  end note
  BR ->> SB : FILE_RESULT (ok = false,\nerror_code = HASH_MISMATCH)
  note over SA, SB
  FAILED,
  session deleted
  end note
  SB ->> AR : FILE_RESULT
  note over AR
  SendSession FAILED
  (HASH_MISMATCH)
  end note
else no relayed message for transfer_timeout (60 s)
  note over SA, SB
  _receive_until_deadline (wakes ≤ 0.5 s)
  → _fail_transfers_of(TIMEOUT, expired_only),
  run by whichever worker wakes first
  end note
  SA ->> AR : ERROR TIMEOUT (transfer_id)
  SA ->> BR : ERROR TIMEOUT (transfer_id)
  note over BR : .part deleted, FAILED
  note over AR : SendSession FAILED
end
note over AR, BR
Each client's reader also puts the ERROR or final snapshot on its
commands queue, so the main thread prints the outcome.
end note
@enduml
